"{
  "ocr_data": "COMMERCIAL INLAND MARINE\nTHIS ENDORSEMENT CHANGES THE CONTRACTORS' EQUIPMENT COVERAGE.\nPLEASE READ IT CAREFULLY\nCONTRACTORS' ELITE INDUSTRY EXTENSION\nThe provisions of the Contractors' Equipment Coverage\nForm apply except as otherwise provided in this\nendorsement. All numbers and letters used to designate\nparagraphs in this endorsement are specific to this\nendorsement only. They do not reference paragraphs in\nthe Contractors' Equipment Coverage Form.\nA. The following additional DEFINITIONS are added:\n1. \"Construction trailer\" means \"your\" transportable\ntrailer or transportable trailer of others in \"your\"\ncare, custody, or control used at \"jobsites\" as an\noffice or storage.\n2. \"Money\" means:\na. Currency, coins, and bank notes in current use\nand having a face value; and\nb. Traveler's checks, register checks and money\norders held for sale to the public.\n3. \"Securities\" means negotiable and non-negotiable\ninstruments or contracts representing either\n\"money\" or other property and includes:\na. Food stamps, lottery tickets, redeemed\ncoupons, tokens, tickets, revenue and other\nstamps (whether represented by actual\nstamps or unused value in a meter) in current\nuse; and\nb. Evidences of debt issued in connection with\ncredit or charge cards, which cards are not\nissued by \"you\".\nB. The following is added to PROPERTY COVERED:\n1. Unscheduled \"Contractors' Equipment\"\na. Coverage - \"We\" cover direct physical loss\ncaused by a covered peril to unscheduled\n\"contractors' equipment\" that \"you\" own.\nb. Coverage Limitation – “We” only cover “your”\nunscheduled “contractors' equipment”:\n(1) When “contractors' equipment” is not\ndescribed as Scheduled Equipment on\nthe “equipment schedule”;\n(2) When “contractors' equipment” is not\nlisted in a schedule which “you” have\nsubmitted to “us” that “we” keep on file\nand when the Schedule on File is\nindicated on the “schedule of coverages”;\nand\n(3) When Supplemental Coverage – Newly\nPurchased Property is not applicable.\nc. Limits –\n(1) The most \"we\" pay for loss to any one\nitem of unscheduled \"contractors'\nequipment\" that \"you\" own is $25,000.\n(2) The most \"we\" pay for loss in any one\noccurrence for all unscheduled\n"contractors' equipment\" that \"you\" own is\n$50,000.\nThe value of unscheduled \"contractors'\n“equipment\" that is owned by \"you\" will be\nthe actual cash value of that property, but\nno more than the \"limits shown in c.(1) and\n(2) in this section.\nC. The following coverages are added to COVERAGE\nEXTENSIONS:\n1. Equipment Leased Or Rented To Others\na. Coverage – “We” cover direct physical loss\ncaused by a covered peril to “your”\n“contractors' equipment” while “you” rent or\nlease it to others.\nb. Property Not Covered – The exclusion for\nLeased Or Rented Property still applies\nexcept to the extent that coverage is\nprovided in this Coverage Extension.\nc. Limit – The most \"we\" pay in any one\noccurrence for loss to all equipment leased\nor rented to others is $100,000.\n2. Equipment Loaned To Others\na. Coverage – “We” pay for direct physical loss\ncaused by a covered peril to covered property\nthat \"you\" loan to other contractors or\nindividuals.\nb. Property Not Covered – The exclusion for\nLoaned Property still applies except to the\nextent that coverage is provided in this\nCoverage Extension.\nc. Coverage Limitation – “We” only cover loss\nto covered property that “you” loan to others\nwhile the property is at a “jobsite” where “you\"\nalso operate.\nCM7508(6-18)\nIncludes copyrighted material of American Association of Insurance Services, Inc., with its permission.\nIncludes copyrighted material of ISO Properties, Inc. with its permission.\nPage 1 of 5",
  "tables": []
}"

"{
  "ocr_data": "d. Limit – The most “we” pay in any one\noccurrence for loss to covered property that\n“you” loan to others is $100,000.\n3. Waterborne Property\na. Coverage – “We” cover direct physical loss\ncaused by a covered peril to covered\nproperty while waterborne.\nb. Property Not Covered – The exclusion for\nWaterborne Property still applies except to\nthe extent that coverage is provided under\nthis Coverage Extension.\nc. Limit – The most “we” pay in any one\noccurrence for loss to covered property\nwhile waterborne is $50,000.\nd. Waterborne Equipment Deductible –\n“We” pay only that part of “your” loss over\nthe deductible amount in any one\noccurrence.\n4. Continuing Rental Or Lease Payments\na. Coverage – In the event of a direct\nphysical loss by a covered peril to covered\n“contractors' equipment” “you” have rented\nor leased, “we” pay for “your” legal liability\nto continue to make rental or lease\npayments for the rented or leased\nequipment after it has been lost or\ndamaged.\nb. Coverage Limitations –\n(1) “We” only pay for “your” rental or lease\npayments:\n(a) If “you” are contractually obligated\nto continue making rental or lease\npayments while the covered\nequipment is repaired or replaced;\nand\n(b) Until the covered equipment has\nbeen repaired or replaced.\n(2) “We” will not pay “you” unless every\nreasonable effort is made to repair,\nreplace, or rebuild the inoperable\nequipment after the loss by a covered\nperil occurs.\nc. Deductible Does Not Apply – The\ndeductible amount indicated on the\n“schedule of coverages” does not apply to\ncontinuing rental or lease payments as\ncovered under this endorsement.\nd. Waiting Period – “We” will not pay “you”\nfor continuing rental or lease payments\nuntil after the first 72 hours following the\ncovered loss to the rented or leased\n“contractors' equipment”.\ne. Incurred Rental Payment – After the waiting\nperiod has passed, “we” will only pay “you”\nfor the continuing rental or lease payments\nthat “you” actually pay.\nf. Coverage After Expiration Date – “We” will\ncontinue to pay “you” for the continuing rental\nor lease payments after the expiration date of\nthis coverage, provided the loss occurred\nbefore the expiration date.\ng. Limits -\n(1) The most “we” pay for continuing rental\nor lease payments for any one piece of\nequipment is $5,000.\n(2) The most “we” pay in any one 12 month\nperiod for all continuing rental or lease\npayments is $25,000.\n5. Fraud and Deceit\na. Coverage – “We” cover theft of covered\nproperty when “you”, “your” agents,\ncustomers, or consignees are fraudulently\ninduced to part with covered property:\n(1) To persons who falsely represent\nthemselves as the proper persons to\nreceive the property;\n(2) By the acceptance of fraudulent bills of\nlading or shipping receipts; or\n(3) As a result of or directly related to the\nuse of any electronic data processing\nhardware or software.\nb. Limit – The most “we” pay in any one\noccurrence for theft of covered property\nunder this Coverage Extension is $50,000.\nD. The following coverages are added to\nSUPPLEMENTAL COVERAGES:\n1. Equipment Borrowed From Others\na. Coverage – “We” cover direct physical loss\ncaused by a covered peril to “contractors'\nequipment” that “you” borrow from another\ncontractor or individual.\nb. Coverage Limitation – “We” only cover loss\nto borrowed equipment that is:\n(1) Similar to “your” “contractors'\nequipment”; and\n(2) Not described on the “equipment\nschedule” or otherwise scheduled.\nc. Limits -\n(1) The most “we” pay for loss to any one\nitem of equipment borrowed from others\nis $100,000.\n(2) The most “we” pay in any one\noccurrence for loss to all equipment\nborrowed from others is $100,000.\nCM7508(6-18)\nIncludes copyrighted material of American Association of Insurance Services, Inc., with its permission\nIncludes copyrighted material of ISO Properties, Inc., with its permission\nPage 2 of 5",
  "tables": []
