"{
  "ocr_data": "COMMERCIAL INLAND MARINE\nCOMMERCIAL OUTPUT POLICY\nIMPORTANT NOTICE TO POLICYHOLDERS\nDISCLOSURE NOTICE – CANNABIS ITEMS AND ACTIVITIES EXCLUSION\nYour policy includes form CL0811 – Cannabis Items\nand Activities Exclusion. This endorsement provides\nadditional clarification concerning coverage for\ncannabis-related property and liability. Please review\nyour policy carefully and contact your agent if you have\nany questions.\nNo coverage is provided by this summary nor does it\nreplace any provisions of your policy. You should read\nyour declarations and policy for complete information\non the coverages you are provided. If there are any\ndiscrepancies between the policy and this summary,\nthe provisions of the policy will govern.\nCANNABIS LEGALITY – Cannabis is a highly\nregulated and restricted substance. As of the effective\ndate of this policy, cannabis is a Schedule 1 drug under\nthe Controlled Substance Act. While individuals in\nsome jurisdictions may be permitted by local laws and\nregulations to engage in certain cannabis activities,\nsuch activities remain illegal at the federal level.\nCLARIFICATION OF CANNABIS COVERAGE – At\ntimes a policy may be interpreted by courts or others as\nproviding coverage or terms that differ from what the\ncompany intends or envisions. Due to differences in\nstate and federal laws regarding the production,\npossession, and use of cannabis items, cannabis-\nrelated coverage has become an issue for which courts\nand policyholders require additional guidance in the\nform of specific cannabis terms, provisions, and\nrestrictions. The following changes clarify policy\nlanguage and preserve the intent of your policy.\nDepending upon the interpretation of your policy, some\nor all of these clarifications may be considered a\nreduction or elimination of coverage. The most\nsignificant of these changes are as follows:\nDefinitions:\n1. Your policy now defines the terms \"cannabis\",\n\"cannabis activities\", and \"cannabis items\".\n2. The term \"cannabis\" includes both cannabis\nplant materials and products derived from such\nmaterials.\n3. The term \"cannabis activities\" is defined as a\nlist of acts performed to or with cannabis.\nHowever, \"cannabis activities\" does not include\n\"cannabis\" use or consumption.\n4. The term \"cannabis items\" includes \"cannabis\"\nas well as \"cannabis\" accessories and\nequipment.\nExclusions:\n1. If the policy provides property coverage, form\nCL0811 excludes coverage for:\n(1) loss to \"cannabis items\"; and\n(2) loss to any other property when the loss\narises out of \"cannabis activities\".\n2. If the policy provides liability coverage, form\nCL0811 excludes coverage for liability arising\nout of:\n(1) the possession of \"cannabis items\"; or\n(2) any \"cannabis activities\".\n3. Neither of the exclusions in form CL0811\napplies to preclude coverage on the basis of\ncannabis use, consumption, or intoxication,\nwhether or not permitted under state law.\nHowever, please be advised that other\nexclusions in your policy may apply.\n4. Neither of the exclusions in form CL0811 is\nintended to modify, narrow, or negate any other\nexclusions found in your policy.\nIL8491(4-19)\nIncludes copyrighted material of American Association of Insurance Services, Inc. with its permission.\nPage 1 of 1",
  "tables": []
