  "ocr_data": "COMMERCIAL AUTO\nCOLORADO POLICYHOLDER NOTICE\nIf the insured's whereabouts for service of process cannot be determined through reasonable effort, the insured\nagrees to designate and irrevocably appoint Employers Mutual Casualty Company as the agent of the insured for\nservice of process, pleadings, or other filings in a civil action brought against the insured or to which the insured has\nbeen joined as a defendant or respondent in any Colorado court if the cause of action concerns an incident for which\nthe insured can possibly claim coverage.\nSubsequent termination of the insurance policy does not affect the appointment for an incident that occurred when\nthe policy was in effect. The insured agrees that any such civil action may be commenced against the insured by the\nservice of process upon Employers Mutual Casualty Company as if personal service had been made directly on\nthe insured. Employers Mutual Casualty Company agrees to forward all communications related to service of\nprocess to the last-known email and mailing address of the policyholder in order to coordinate payment of claims or\ndefense of claims that are required.\nCA8214(5-12)\nPage 1 of 1",
