  "ocr_data": "CYBERSOLUTIONS\nIMPORTANT NOTICE TO POLICYHOLDERS\nThis Notice summarizes coverage changes that may affect your Data Compromise Coverage Form. No coverage is\nprovided by this summary nor does it replace any provision of your policy. You should read your policy including all\nendorsements and review your declarations page for complete information on the coverage you are provided. If there\nis any conflict between the policy and this notice, THE PROVISIONS OF THE POLICY SHALL PREVAIL. This notice\ncontains a brief synopsis of the significant broadenings, restrictions and clarifications of coverage that were made to\nyour existing coverage form. Please contact your agent to discuss any questions. Your right to cancel remains\nunchanged.\nPLEASE READ YOUR POLICY, AND THE ENDORSEMENTS ATTACHED TO YOUR POLICY, CAREFULLY.\nCyberSolutions Coverage Form - DC7001(1-17)\nCyberSolutions Coverage Form – DC7001.1(1-17)\nBROADENING IN COVERAGE:\nData Compromise\n• Additional coverages provided for Regulatory Fines & Penalties (where allowed by law).\n• Additional coverages provided for PCI Fines & Penalties (where allowed by law).\n• Data Compromise Liability coverage changed to claims-made and regulatory defense coverage added.\n• Data Compromise Liability now provides for an Extended Reporting Period.\n• The exclusion for data transmitted electronically has been removed.\n• Forensic IT sublimit and Legal Review sublimit were increased to 50% of the Data Compromise Response\nExpenses limit.\n• Public Relations sublimit was increased to $10,000.\nCyber\n• New Cyber Extortion coverage has been added to the Computer Attack coverage, with its own sublimit.\n• Data Re-creation sublimit has been removed.\n• New Electronic Media Liability coverage has been added.\n• Computer Attack coverage has been increased to include an authorized person accessing a computer system\nfor unauthorized purposes.\n• Loss of Business – sublimit increased to 50% of Computer Attack limit.\n• Public Relations sublimit was increased to $10,000.\nIdentity Recovery\n• Standard Identity Recovery deductible has been removed and is no longer applicable to this coverage.\nDeductibles\n• All Cyber deductibles have been lowered and now match current deductibles we have available under Data\nCompromise coverage. Multiple Cyber deductible options have been eliminated and each annual aggregate\nlimit has a specific deductible.\nCLARIFICATIONS AND OTHER CHANGES IN COVERAGE:\n• All coverages are available in a single form. Identity Recovery Coverage Form has now been integrated within\nCyberSolutions Coverage Form. It is still automatically included when Data Compromise coverage is selected.\n• $25,000 Data Compromise or Cyber annual aggregate limit is no longer available. Minimum available limit\nnow is $50,000. All policies with $25,000 limit are automatically rolled into a $50,000 limit.\n• New policy definitions have been added or deleted either as clarification or due to addition of new coverages\nmentioned previously. Following definitions were revised:\n• “Affected Individual” now also includes a patient and a student.\n• “Business Income” was deleted and replaced with “Business Income and Extra Expense\".\n• \"Period of Restoration” was deleted and incorporated within “Business Income and Extra Expense\"\ndefinition.\nDC8005(4-17)\nPage 1 of 1",
